# Package-level .gitattributes
#
# Mirrors the LFS rules from the repository-root .gitattributes so that Unity
# Package Manager (UPM) git URL resolution picks them up reliably. The root
# .gitattributes alone is NOT sufficient when packages are fetched through
# UPM with a `?path=<package-dir>` extension -- in that mode UPM only reads
# attributes scoped to (or inside) the package directory.
#
# Background: Unity Issue Tracker #1256330 ("Package Manager fails to
# download LFS files from Git repository when the Git URL contains a path
# extension"). Officially marked Fixed, but regressions have been reported
# on 2021.3 / 2022.3 / Unity 6 -- without a package-local .gitattributes,
# LFS-tracked binaries (e.g. Tools~/VirgoMotionFusion/VirgoMotionFusion.exe)
# come down as 134-byte pointer text files in `Library/PackageCache`, and
# any Process.Start on them fails with Win32 ERROR_BAD_EXE_FORMAT.
#
# Macro attributes ([attr]...) MUST NOT appear here -- nested .gitattributes
# files cannot define macros (Git LFS docs). Keep every rule inline.
#
# Keep this file in sync with the relevant subset of the repository-root
# .gitattributes whenever LFS-tracked extensions change.

# Unity binary assets
*.bin filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.anim filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.unitypackage filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.apk filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.assets filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

